course: dictionary
lesson: 14123
title: Midway
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Midway means in the middle, halfway between two places or two points in time. Look at the words around it to check. «We stopped for a drink midway up the hill.» The stop was not at the bottom or the top, so midway must mean halfway.
explain: Midway can also describe time. «The film had a surprise midway through.» A surprise in the middle of a film comes halfway through it, not at the start or the end. Midway through is a useful phrase to remember.
explain: In maths, midway tells you the midpoint. Midway between 4 and 10 is 7, because 4 plus 10 is 14 and half of 14 is 7. Try the swap check: put halfway in place of midway, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Midway means halfway, in the middle of two places or two points in time.
fact: Phrases to learn: midway through, midway between, and midway point.
fact: «Midway» can also mean the area at a fair with rides, games and food stalls, in the US and Canada.
fact: The Midway Atoll is in the Pacific Ocean, and it was the site of a famous sea battle in 1942.
fact: The Battle of Midway in 1942 was a turning point in the Second World War in the Pacific.
exercise: «We stopped for a rest midway through the walk.» What does midway mean here? | At the very end of the walk | Far away from the walk | *In the middle of the walk | Before the walk began
exercise: Midway between 4 and 10 is which number? | 8 | 14 | *7 | 6
exercise: «The fair had rides, games and food stalls on the midway.» In the US and Canada, what is the midway? | A type of race track | A small island in the sea | A bridge over a river | *The area with rides and games at a fair
test: «The story reached its exciting part midway through the book.» Where did the exciting part happen? | At the start | *In the middle | Never | At the very end
test: Which word means halfway between two places? | *Midway | Famished | Ancient | Curt
exam: «The Battle of Midway» in 1942 was a famous sea battle in the Pacific. What is it? | A mountain in the Pacific Ocean | *A famous sea battle in the Pacific in 1942 | A type of maths sum | A fair with rides and games
